    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Explicit authored prerequisite restatement:\nFull finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0; source V C2 and NNReal0<alpha<=beta with true all-point/all-vector alphaI<=HessV<=betaI, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1.\nActual common Gaussian J=(x,x+sqrteta*xi)#(mu*standardGaussian), Markov/disintegrating R and reflected S_y=(2x-y)#R_y; actual W_y(z)=V((y+z)/2)+norm(z-y)^2/(8eta), S_y=volume.tilted(-W_y), integrable/positive partition. SAME dense closable exact original D_y precedes ALL constants/domain elements/directions.\nActual unnormalized parameter-y score s_y(u)[a]=-DV((y+u)/2)[a]/2-inner(y-u,a)/(4eta), not the negative u-gradient or already centered normalized score. Its C1/scalarL2/boundedgradient is produced by the accepted score theorem; only literal S2_y=S_y from exact density is used.\nConstruct true common conditional J/R/S, positive reflected C2 potential and SAME original D_y before ALL c/u/a. Produce actual constant domain, full kernel equality and actual noncompact unnormalized directional-y score C1/gradient bound with true scalar/vector L2 class pair in SAME D_y.closure.graph. No R2/R identity or alternate operator is assumed.\nActual finite real Hilbert/Borel E including0. Fix actual finite mu and SAME original closable exact compact-C-infinity gradient D BEFORE ALL C1 f with actual MemLp f2mu and MemLp gradientf2mu. Genuine smooth cutoff exhaustion/derivative-product/weighted L2 limits put actual class pair into SAME closure graph, without compact support or extra spatial moment. Finite mu constants are genuinely in original closure domain with outputzero. For actual C1 Gibbs W/exp(-W) integrable, combine actual constants-domain with accepted one-way implication for full zero-output iff AEconstant on SAME D. Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/Sdensity/positive partitions/sourceC2 alpha beta eta cap and original D_y beforeALL constants/u/directions; real unnormalized y-score C1/L2/boundedgradient from accepted score producer transfers along ONLY explicit reflected density equality S2_y=S_y and enters SAME original closed graph. No R2=R or alternateD equality, global ordinary L1, C-infinity potential, gradient of rough representative, Nontrivial E, spatial moment, supplied domain/fullkernel/spectralgap/Poincare certificate, epsilon0/range/centering/measurablejointselector/core/BL/main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded cost.",
    "text_sha256": "7a2883596c602aa71a3623f6f54d9c8b4606622c26cab2587f2a61c89f66ca1a"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalScoreClosedDomain.conditional_score_closed_gradient_domain",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ConditionalScoreClosedDomain.lean",
    "statement": "{V : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α:ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α:ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β:ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β:ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := Measure.map (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2)) (μ.prod (stdGaussian E))\n    let W := fun y u : E => V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) + ‖u-y‖^2/(8*η)\n    let s := fun y u : E => -(1/2:ℝ) • fderiv ℝ V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) -\n      (1/(4*η)) • innerSL ℝ (y-u)\n    ∃ R S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel R ∧ IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (J.map Prod.swap).IsCondKernel R ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x => (2:ℝ) • x-y)) ∧\n      ∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -W y u) ∧\n        ContDiff ℝ 2 (W y) ∧ Integrable (fun u => Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        0 < (∫ u, Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        ∃ D : Lp ℝ 2 (S y) →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 (S y),\n          Dense (D.domain : Set (Lp ℝ 2 (S y))) ∧ D.IsClosable ∧ D.closure.IsClosed ∧\n          (∀ (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) (v : Lp E 2 (S y)), (u,v) ∈ D.graph ↔\n            ∃ f : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ f ∧ HasCompactSupport f ∧\n              u =ᵐ[S y] f ∧ v =ᵐ[S y] gradient f) ∧\n          (∀ c : ℝ, ∃ u : D.closure.domain,\n            (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) =ᵐ[S y] (fun _ => c) ∧ D.closure u=0) ∧\n          (∀ u : D.closure.domain, D.closure u=0 ↔\n            ∃ c : ℝ, (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) =ᵐ[S y] (fun _ => c)) ∧\n          ∀ a : E, ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun u => s y u a) ∧\n            (∀ u, ‖gradient (fun z => s y z a) u‖ ≤ ((1/η-(α:ℝ))/4)*‖a‖) ∧\n            ∃ hp : MemLp (fun u => s y u a) 2 (S y),\n              ∃ hq : MemLp (gradient (fun u => s y u a)) 2 (S y),\n                (hp.toLp _,hq.toLp _) ∈ D.closure.graph",
    "statement_sha256": "0d4220c713c888cc4324da1bbfe95ee307e83ff75d7d225a43131abb9adbeeeb",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "Full finite real Hilbert/Borel E with canonical full-space volume, including0. Finite actual mu and same original closable compact-smooth gradient D before all C1 inputs/classes.",
      "C1 f and genuine scalar/vector gradient MemLp2 are actual hypotheses; finite probability alone does not make an unbounded f L2. No compact support, global volumeL1 or norm(x)*f moment is required.",
      "Real radial cutoff exhaustion with true product Frechet derivative and weighted quotient L2 limits enters SAME original closure graph. Neither representative convergence alone nor supplied domain/density certificate substitutes for the actual proof.",
      "Finite mu constants have real zero gradient and actual domain witness/output0; not assumed. For actual C1 W and integrable exp(-W), normalized Gibbs full zero-output iff AEconstant combines this with accepted positive-density one-way implication. No spectralgap/Poincare follows.",
      "Actual PBPS common Gaussian J/R/S/reflection/positive normalized W_y and original dense D_y precede ALL constants/u/directions. Source C2 alpha/beta eta cap, exact quarter Hessian/reflected scale and dimension0 retained. No alternate D is chosen per input.",
      "Actual s_y(u)[a]=-DV((y+u)/2)[a]/2-inner(y-u,a)/(4eta) is the unnormalized parameter-y directional score, not negative u-gradient or centered normalized score. Existing producer gives C1/scalarL2/boundedgradient. Only S2_y=S_y via literal normalized reflected density equality is used; no R2/R identity.",
      "Full first-order constant kernel equality is admitted by the stated new theorem; centered residual/epsilon0/range/Poincare/BL/roughHessian/adjoint/core/main/composition remain open. No measurablejointfiberselector or TV unbounded-cost transfer."
